WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.287
A pivot can aggregate revenue instead of counts.

00:00:03.287 --> 00:00:05.812
This query groups by sale month.

00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:09.602
Each filtered SUM collects revenue for one product.

00:00:09.602 --> 00:00:16.617
The result has one row per month and separate revenue columns for Laptop, Mouse, and Keyboard.

00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:22.002
Always identify both the output grain and the measure being aggregated.

00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:29.272
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:29.272 --> 00:00:32.817
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:32.817 --> 00:00:39.042
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:39.864
combination.
